rows=[
('How many ordinary turns does each player take in the standard 16-round game, and what happens (including service rotation and ongoing tile benefits) on a courtship round?', 'Twelve ordinary turns: four seasons, each three ordinary rounds then a courtship. No player turn, rotation, monument reputation or Servants’ Hall use on courtship; only courtship resolves.', 'pp.16,76; extraction lines 614–629,2898–2903'),
('State the ordered procedure for hosting an activity, including when round-track events and ongoing effects happen and where used servants, gentry and the tile go at cleanup.', 'Rotate service; resolve round event then ongoing effects; choose activity; invite exact required gentry; provide service; enjoy favours; optional market buy; clear board. Used servants to Expended Service, played gentry to personal discard, tile upgraded if needed and returned to correct tableau column; last player advances marker.', 'pp.17–20; lines 642–796'),
('When passing, in what order do you recover servants and gentry, resolve events/ongoing effects, take a passing benefit and buy? What benefits are available in this base-only scope, and may you hire through Butler’s Room as a passing benefit?', 'All servants directly Available; all personal discard gentry to hand; round event then ongoing effects; choose £200 or free market refresh; optional one tile purchase; last player advances marker. Hiring on pass is expansion/optional and excluded here.', 'p.21,30; lines 801–830,1135–1144'),
('Your reputation is 6.1 after step 2 and you plan a PR6 activity with PR6 guests, but need four Service Help actions that lower your actual reputation to 3.4. Is this legal, which servants can Service Help refresh, and what reputation is used to screen the tile and guests?', 'Legal if four needed servants are in Servants’ Quarters and costs payable. Service Help costs 3 increments each, Quarters to Available only. Screening reputation fixed after step 2 before step 3 is level 6 for tile and guests all turn; later loss does not invalidate.', 'pp.18,27,77; lines 705–724,1057–1062,2922–2932'),
('How must positive and negative favours be ordered? At minimum reputation can you take a negative reputation favour first to avoid the loss, and what is required to play a guest with a money penalty?', 'All positive before all negative. Cannot take loss first at minimum; ignore only loss beyond minimum after positives. Must pay money penalty; activity income, VP money or Borrow Money can fund it. If unable to fund full payment cannot play guest.', 'pp.36,76–77; lines 1379–1391,2905–2924'),
('Give all three special action costs, their per-turn limits and the minimum-reputation restriction. Can service help take a servant straight out of Expended Service?', 'Borrow £100 costs 2 increments, repeatable; Service Help 3 increments per servant Quarters to Available, repeatable; Refresh Market 4 increments, special action once per turn. Need enough reputation; no specials at minimum 1.1. No direct refresh from Expended via Service Help.', 'p.27; lines 1043–1062'),
('How do you hire with the base Butler’s Room activity, may any gentry attend, where do new hires go, and how does upgrading change the recruiting option?', 'Use available butler/underbutler, no gentry. Take up to two from Servants for Hire except underbutler to Expended Service; used butler also expended and tile upgrades. Upgraded room may instead recruit one common footman/valet/lady’s maid from anywhere on one opponent board to your Expended, never unique servants.', 'pp.29–30,88; lines 1076–1084,1110–1144,3357–3374'),
('When may a housekeeper substitute for a lady’s maid, when may a footman substitute for a valet, and can an underbutler substitute while the regular male servant is still available?', 'Housekeeper only no available lady’s maid; footman requires Brushing Room and no available valet. Underbutler may replace butler/valet/footman even if regular available.', 'pp.29–30,88; lines 1091–1105,1117–1134,3351–3356'),
('How can an underbutler be acquired in the base game, when is it available, and can another player recruit it?', 'Only acquire Butler’s Pantry; gain underbutler from supply immediately into Expended Service. Cannot hire with Butler’s Room or hire-servant VP card; unique, cannot be recruited.', 'pp.29–30,88,105; lines 1097–1105,1140–1143,3351–3356,3973–3977'),
('How is a tile’s purchase price calculated in the Market and Reserve, what is the minimum price, and can you buy a tile you already own or one above your reputation?', 'Market space price plus tile modifier; Reserve £300 plus modifier; minimum £100. Cannot acquire duplicates by any means. May purchase above reputation; PR restricts play only.', 'pp.26,40; lines 1005–1010,1524–1546'),
('When refilling the Market after a purchase, what happens to remaining tiles, a drawn duplicate, a reserve-eligible tile and multiple newly drawn tiles? Does buying just one tile from a duplicate stack cause a refill?', 'Slide remaining left; stack drawn duplicate on match and draw again; qualifying Service/PR1 drawn tile to Reserve and draw again; sort new tiles by ascending sorting number when filling multiple spaces. One remaining duplicate keeps space occupied so no refill.', 'pp.20,41; lines 770–777,1550–1557'),
('After seasons 1 and 2, which Market tiles move to Reserve, what exception applies, what happens to later draws, and is a full seasonal Market refresh standard here?', 'After season1 all Service except Largest Wine Cellar; after season2 PR1. Later eligible draws go straight Reserve. Full Market refresh after first three courtships standard under compendium/corrigendum; old stable-market aid incomplete.', 'pp.23,40–41; corrigendum p.2; lines 884–920,1524–1531,4569–4572'),
('For an ordinary (nonfinal) courtship, how are Fairchilds returned, theme scores and ties handled, and objectives discarded? Which direction does the first-player marker then pass?', 'Return both Fairchilds first. Total current theme-category tile VP including negatives; highest draws VP and chooses one Fairchild to hand. Ties all draw VP and no Fairchild. Each discards one objective face down; shuffle together and bottom objective deck. At season setup first player passes anticlockwise.', 'pp.22–23; lines 835–879,902–909'),
('How does final courtship differ in scoring and tie resolution, and what last actions are permitted before end-game scoring?', 'Sum tile VP in all four revealed theme categories, repeated categories count repeatedly/double for two. Highest wins Fairchild+VP; tied highest reputation level breaks tie ignoring wheel position; if still tied no Fairchild, tied winners draw VP. After courtship final special actions and VP-card benefits if possible, then scoring.', 'pp.22–24,42; lines 860–870,884–897,1604–1609'),
('List all end-game VP categories, the points for reputation levels 1–7, wealth rounding, and the complete victory tiebreak sequence.', 'Tiles including negative; gentry in hand/discard incl final Fairchild and negatives; remaining objectives; reputation 1,3,6,10,15,21,28 for levels1–7; servants2 each; £200 per1VP rounded down; unused VP cards. Tie: final Fairchild holder, then highest rep level ignoring position, then shared victory.', 'p.24; lines 926–954'),
('How many objectives do you normally receive and retain for scoring in a standard game, what happens to simultaneous discards, and must tile objectives show upgraded tiles?', '5 setup+2 Draw Objectives=7; discard1 each of4 courtships leaves3. Shuffle simultaneous face-down discards before bottom deck. Extra objective effects increase final total by1 each. Tile objectives require possession at end, no upgrade required.', 'pp.42,77,106; lines 1592–1623,2935–2940,4000–4001'),
('When can VP cards be used for benefits, where do used cards go, and what happens to retained cards at game end?', 'Immediately on draw or anytime own turn; final chance after final courtship. Reveal and discard to bottom VP deck for benefit; may use several. Retain hidden with objectives and score printed VP if not discarded; no both benefit and VP.', 'pp.22,42; lines 865–871,1592–1609'),
('Explain the mandatory flip rules for a normal activity tile, an already-upgraded tile, a hybrid, and a tile that upgrades into an ongoing monument. Which category counts for a hybrid at courtship and for objectives?', 'First use normal tile flips to upgrade at cleanup, mandatory; upgraded stays. Hybrid flips each use and moves correct category, starts underlined hybrid icon side. Activity-to-monument flips after first use and never hosts again. Only currently face-up hybrid category counts.', 'pp.20,39; lines 785–793,1473–1505'),
('When do monuments and Servants’ Hall work on a hosting turn and a pass turn? How does Servants’ Hall use a servant, and may it target a player at minimum reputation?', 'After event in step2 hosting or step3 pass. Monuments1rep per ordinary turn, no courtship. Hall any one available servant on tile to lower opponent1 gain1; used servant expended end turn; still host activity/pass. Cannot target minimum-rep opponent.', 'pp.17–18,21,27,39,101; lines 681–685,810–811,1046–1051,1473–1489,3824–3831'),
('Compare Heritage Guest Suite, Queen’s Suite and Lionheart Suite: which guest is used, service and doubling rules, subsequent tile state, and whether their single-guest count can be changed.', 'Heritage one casual from hand, footman tile and guest normal service; double all favours including negative, stays upgraded activity. Queen one prestige from hand, housekeeper tile and normal guest service; double1 chosen favour others normal; upgrades monument. Lionheart butler tile draws1 prestige from deck no guest service, double all nonnegative favours, keep guest to discard; upgrades monument. All fixed1 cannot modify count.', 'pp.79,93,95,99; lines 3010–3014,3532–3535,3605–3614,3765–3771')]
